        <div style="font-size: 20px; color: #0e1c42; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 10px;">One state sent its sons to fight more than a thousand miles apart: in the woods of Virginia, and on the bayous and borders of the Trans-Mississippi.</div>
        <div style="font-size: 18px; color: #1a2340; line-height: 1.65;">When the war began, thousands of Texans joined the Confederate army. Some marched east to fight in Lee&rsquo;s army. Others stayed to fight in the West, or to guard Texas itself. You will follow Texans on both fronts and see how the war came home.</div>
